WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.634
-My next guests are the stars

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:06.534
of the biggest television show
in the world, "Squid Game."

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:09.133
It is streaming now on Netflix.

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:12.868
Here are Lee Jung-jae,
Park Hae-soo,

00:00:12.868 --> 00:00:15.868
Wi Ha-Joon, and Jung Hoyeon!

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:21.467
Welcome! Yes! Yes!

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:24.534
Welcome, welcome, welcome!

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.501
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:26.501 --> 00:00:28.501
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:28.501 --> 00:00:30.968
-[ Speaking native language ]
-Thank you.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.634
-Thank you.
-Thank you for having us.

00:00:32.634 --> 00:00:34.200
-This is a big deal.

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.601
I just want to start.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:38.067
Jung-jae, you're the first one
we meet in the show,

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:41.868
and you're so charming
and, like, lovable.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:43.267
We're rooting for you.

00:00:43.267 --> 00:00:44.934
I know that
you're famous in Korea

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:49.067
for mostly playing villains
in a movie.

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:53.534
How can that face be a villain?
You're so friendly and likable.

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:56.167
Can you tell everyone
what "Squid Game" is about?

00:00:56.167 --> 00:00:58.100
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:01:15.734 --> 00:01:19.968
-It's frightening.
It is shocking.

00:01:19.968 --> 00:01:22.467
But it's also really beautiful,

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:27.200
and right now it is number one
on Netflix in 90 countries.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.868 --> 00:01:32.300
It is bigger than --

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:38.400
Uh, Hae-soo, when did you
realize the show became so big?

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.033
-Right now.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:45.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.801
-Right now?
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:01:46.801 --> 00:01:49.267
Yeah, right now.

00:01:58.467 --> 00:02:01.100
I want to meet Jimmy...

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.601
[ Audience awws ]

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:06.367
-That's what I'm talking about.
See? This is...

00:02:06.367 --> 00:02:08.400
That's my man.
I love you. Come on.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.601
Oh. I'm so happy.

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:12.934
Ha-Joon, what do you think

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:16.000
people around the world
are connecting to?

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.968
-Ohh...

00:02:17.968 --> 00:02:20.400
[ Speaking native language ]

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:42.033
-Yeah, it is --
it's bizarre how --

00:02:42.033 --> 00:02:43.701
the combo of that.

00:02:43.701 --> 00:02:46.567
The children's game,
but also people desperate

00:02:46.567 --> 00:02:48.968
kind of to just change
their life and get money.

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:54.133
And they'll do -- And it starts
with the creepiest doll I've --

00:02:54.133 --> 00:02:57.133
And I have to show you,
for people who haven't seen.

00:02:57.133 --> 00:03:00.901
I got this sent over to us.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.033
This came in the mail.

00:03:02.033 --> 00:03:03.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:06.200
This came in the mail for me.
Yeah, thank you so much.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:07.701
Wait. No.
If you haven't seen this...

00:03:07.701 --> 00:03:09.367
Wait. Watch this. This is --

00:03:09.367 --> 00:03:10.968
So, this is what --

00:03:10.968 --> 00:03:12.701
They played
Red Light, Green Light,

00:03:12.701 --> 00:03:16.033
but this giant doll
looks at them, okay?

00:03:16.033 --> 00:03:19.634
And she says, "Green light,"
and her head is turned around.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:21.267
When she says, "Red light,"

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.267
she turns around,
and her eyes are cameras.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:25.501
And if you move, you get shot.

00:03:25.501 --> 00:03:27.467
[ Laughs ]

00:03:27.467 --> 00:03:29.033
But -- I know.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:33.634
But, also, this robot
is based on a character, right?

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.467
From Korean textbooks.

00:03:35.467 --> 00:03:38.367
Like, when kids are growing up,
you know who this --

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:42.400
Who is this?
Who is this psycho robot?

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:44.334
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.334 --> 00:03:50.133
-When we were at the school,
there were, like, characters.

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:53.334
One is a boy,
and one is the girl.

00:03:53.334 --> 00:03:56.667
The boy's name was Chulsoo,

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:59.467
and the girl's name
was Younghee.

00:03:59.467 --> 00:04:01.334
And she's the one.

00:04:01.334 --> 00:04:02.767
-Whew. Yeah.

00:04:02.767 --> 00:04:05.634
Jung-jae,
this show is pretty dark,

00:04:05.634 --> 00:04:10.167
but your character
is optimistic and funny.

00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.100
And I was just wondering,
is there anything

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:14.267
that didn't make it to the show
that was --

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.701
or maybe things that were in the
show that were improvised?

00:04:16.701 --> 00:04:18.634
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:18.634 --> 00:04:20.434
[ Speaking native language ]

00:04:54.367 --> 00:04:56.167
-I remember that scene. The --

00:04:56.167 --> 00:04:58.567
It's in the first episode.
No spoilers.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:01.868
I'm not giving any spoilers
tonight, so everyone knows.

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:04.634
Hae-soo, you became a dad

00:05:04.634 --> 00:05:06.734
the day "Squid Game" premiered.

00:05:06.734 --> 00:05:08.000
Is that correct?

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.100
[ Applause ]

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.968
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.033
-Baby Squid.

00:05:45.834 --> 00:05:47.133
[ Applause ]

00:05:47.133 --> 00:05:51.701
-Yeah! Little Baby Squid!
How cute! Come on!

00:05:51.701 --> 00:05:55.701
I want to show everyone
a clip from the show.

00:05:55.701 --> 00:05:58.434
This is "Squid Game."
Take a look.

00:05:58.434 --> 00:06:01.901
-♪ In other words ♪

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:06.300
♪ Darling, kiss me ♪

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.701
♪ Fill my heart with song ♪

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:13.701
♪ And let me sing forever more ♪

00:06:13.701 --> 00:06:16.400
♪ You are all I long for ♪

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.367
♪ All I worship and adore ♪

00:06:20.367 --> 00:06:23.334
♪ In other words ♪

00:06:23.334 --> 00:06:27.367
♪ Please be true ♪

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:30.234
♪ In other words ♪

00:06:30.234 --> 00:06:33.167
[ Music stops ]

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:35.367
-[ Breathing sharply ]

00:06:35.367 --> 00:06:37.067
-Ohh!

00:06:37.067 --> 00:06:38.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.701 --> 00:06:41.334
He saved you! I love it!

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.634
The cast of "Squid Game,"
everybody!

00:06:43.634 --> 00:06:45.834
The show is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:06:45.834 --> 00:06:48.467
"Squid Game" is all about
playing childhood games,

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:50.701
so I thought we could have
some fun with that.

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:53.100
You're about to face off
against each other

00:06:53.100 --> 00:06:55.300
in the "Tonight Show
Schoolyard Games."

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.734
Here we go.

00:06:56.734 --> 00:07:00.167
-♪ Schoolyard Games, ooh, yeah ♪

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:03.534
-Now, the games will now begin.

00:07:03.534 --> 00:07:07.501
All will play,
but only one can win.

00:07:07.501 --> 00:07:10.200
Round one, Slapsies.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.367
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:14.400
[ Applause ]

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.701
This is the game where you do
this over each other's hands.

00:07:17.701 --> 00:07:21.100
You can kind of fake out,
but if you fake out

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.634
and you flinch and move all
the way back, you slap the hand.

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:25.767
But if you can do it
fast enough and just go like --

00:07:25.767 --> 00:07:26.934
wa-psh!

00:07:26.934 --> 00:07:28.467
That's Slapsies, yeah.

00:07:28.467 --> 00:07:29.634
Yeah.
It might not be called that.

00:07:29.634 --> 00:07:31.133
We might have made up
the name "Slapsies."

00:07:31.133 --> 00:07:33.234
But that's the game.

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:36.501
Jung-jae, Hae-soo,
you're up first.

00:07:36.501 --> 00:07:39.267
On your mark.

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:40.767
Get set.

00:07:40.767 --> 00:07:42.934
-[ Speaking native language ]
-Go.

00:07:42.934 --> 00:07:45.133
♪♪

00:07:45.133 --> 00:07:46.434
-Whoa!

00:07:46.434 --> 00:07:48.734
-Wow.
-Yeah.

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:49.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.901 --> 00:07:51.067
[ Bell dings ]

00:07:51.067 --> 00:07:52.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.000
-Hae-soo, you won that one.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:55.701
[ Laughs ]

00:07:55.701 --> 00:07:58.467
Not at the whole game.
Not at the whole game.

00:07:58.467 --> 00:07:59.834
Okay.

00:07:59.834 --> 00:08:02.200
Ha-Joon, Hoyeon, you're up next.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.734
♪♪

00:08:03.734 --> 00:08:05.501
-[ Speaking native language ]
-Okay.

00:08:05.501 --> 00:08:08.334
-[ Speaking native language ]
I want to...

00:08:08.334 --> 00:08:10.234
-Three, two, one.

00:08:10.234 --> 00:08:11.501
♪♪

00:08:11.501 --> 00:08:14.100
Yeah! Oh, my God! Yeah!

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.901
First try!

00:08:15.901 --> 00:08:17.367
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:08:17.367 --> 00:08:20.801
-All right. That means we go
to the final round right here.

00:08:20.801 --> 00:08:24.133
Hae-soo, Hoyeon,
you are up against each other.

00:08:24.133 --> 00:08:26.901
Yeah. Good --
Best of luck. Yeah.

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:28.334
This is what I'm talking about.

00:08:30.067 --> 00:08:32.501
-All right. One, two, three.

00:08:32.501 --> 00:08:34.601
♪♪

00:08:34.601 --> 00:08:35.834
[ Bell dings ]

00:08:35.834 --> 00:08:37.767
-[ Laughs ]

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.601
Are you okay?
-Congratulations.

00:08:39.601 --> 00:08:41.467
It is time for the next round.

00:08:41.467 --> 00:08:44.267
And things aren't
going to get any easier.

00:08:44.267 --> 00:08:46.734
Because you're about to play
one of the most dangerous games

00:08:46.734 --> 00:08:50.033
of all --
Rock, Paper, Scissors.

00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:53.267
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:08:53.267 --> 00:08:55.567
Jung-jae, Hae-soo,
you are up first.

00:08:55.567 --> 00:08:56.834
Rock, Paper, Scissors.

00:08:56.834 --> 00:09:00.801
Whenever you're ready,
you can go.

00:09:00.801 --> 00:09:02.467
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:09:04.734 --> 00:09:07.434
-[ Bell dings ]
-Jung-jae!

00:09:07.434 --> 00:09:09.934
Jung-jae is the winner
of that one.

00:09:09.934 --> 00:09:14.601
Ha-Joon, Hoyeon, you're up now.

00:09:14.601 --> 00:09:17.501
-Both:
Rock, paper, scissor!

00:09:17.501 --> 00:09:19.267
-Okay.
-There's two scissors.

00:09:19.267 --> 00:09:21.033
-Rock, paper, scissor!

00:09:21.033 --> 00:09:22.467
-No!

00:09:22.467 --> 00:09:25.167
-[ Bell dings ]
-Here we go!

00:09:25.167 --> 00:09:30.267
Now, Jung-jae, Ha-Joon,
you guys have to go head-to-head

00:09:30.267 --> 00:09:31.934
rock, paper, scissors

00:09:31.934 --> 00:09:33.534
to see who the winner
of this match is.

00:09:33.534 --> 00:09:34.934
Here we go.
I know. Look at this.

00:09:34.934 --> 00:09:37.567
Whew. Gear up.

00:09:37.567 --> 00:09:39.834
Mentally focus.
When you're ready. Yeah.

00:09:39.834 --> 00:09:42.400
-[ Speaking native language ]

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:43.701
-[ Bell dings ]
-Oh, yes!

00:09:43.701 --> 00:09:45.567
That's what I'm talking about
right there!

00:09:45.567 --> 00:09:48.501
Ha-Joon! Congratulations, bud!

00:09:48.501 --> 00:09:50.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:50.667 --> 00:09:54.234
All right. We've now reached
the final round.

00:09:54.234 --> 00:09:56.467
This determines
the winner of everything.

00:09:56.467 --> 00:09:58.267
But before we play, each of you

00:09:58.267 --> 00:10:01.567
must pick a number
between 1 and 4.

00:10:01.567 --> 00:10:03.167
[ Laughter ]

00:10:03.167 --> 00:10:05.567
♪♪

00:10:05.567 --> 00:10:09.234
-I will go...number two.

00:10:09.234 --> 00:10:11.100
-Three.

00:10:11.100 --> 00:10:14.400
-Okay.
-Four.

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:15.934
-One.
-One.

00:10:15.934 --> 00:10:17.367
-Yeah, you have no choice.
You have no choice.

00:10:17.367 --> 00:10:18.734
You're one. Okay, here we go.

00:10:18.734 --> 00:10:22.467
Now that your numbers are
locked in, the game may begin.

00:10:22.467 --> 00:10:25.467
It is time
for Egg and Spoon Race.

00:10:25.467 --> 00:10:29.267
[ Dramatic music plays ]

00:10:29.267 --> 00:10:32.000
But not all spoons
are created equal.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.601
The number you choose
determines your spoon.

00:10:34.601 --> 00:10:37.868
Please take the spoon
that matches your number.

00:10:37.868 --> 00:10:40.000
-Ah.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:41.934
-What is number two?

00:10:41.934 --> 00:10:43.801
-Three.
-Number two!

00:10:43.801 --> 00:10:46.033
Yeah! Number two!
-Yeah, that's a good one.

00:10:46.033 --> 00:10:48.167
-[ Laughs ] Four. One.

00:10:48.167 --> 00:10:50.234
-Oh, no. Oh, no.

00:10:50.234 --> 00:10:53.067
One, you got --
You have a tough --

00:10:53.067 --> 00:10:55.167
[ Laughs ] Oh, my gosh.

00:10:57.033 --> 00:11:01.200
Oh, no. Oh, no. Okay.
Oh, no. All right.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:05.167
When you're ready, take your
places and get ready to race.

00:11:05.167 --> 00:11:07.934
The first person
to cross the finish line

00:11:07.934 --> 00:11:11.067
with an intact egg
is the winner.

00:11:13.367 --> 00:11:15.868
On your mark. Get set.

00:11:15.868 --> 00:11:17.801
-On my mark.

00:11:17.801 --> 00:11:19.234
-Go!

00:11:19.234 --> 00:11:21.133
-Aah!

00:11:21.133 --> 00:11:24.901
-Ohh! Hey! All right.

00:11:24.901 --> 00:11:28.133
Jung-jae. Jung-jae, you get it.
But you know what?

00:11:28.133 --> 00:11:29.467
You're all winners.

